            <ArticleTitle>Chelation therapy of atherosclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1000-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chelation therapy with intravenous injections of edetate disodium is being promoted to the public as a nonsurgical means to treat coronary or other arterial atherosclerosis. The rationale for use, clinical efficacy, and safety are reviewed. Acceptable evidence supporting chelation therapy for atherosclerotic vascular disease is lacking.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
